---
{
  title: "settle_async"
}
---
### NAME

    settle_async() - Applies an async function to every element of an array
    at once and reports how each one ended.

### SYNOPSIS

    async varargs mapping *settle_async( mixed *src, function fun, mixed extra... );

### DESCRIPTION

    Applies an async function to every element of an array at once and
    reports how each one ended.

    map_async() for the case where a failure is an outcome to record rather
    than an error to abandon the batch for. Nothing rejects: every element
    produces an entry, positionally matching src, in promise_status()'s
    vocabulary:

    ([ "status": PROMISE_FULFILLED, "value": v ]) ([ "status":
    PROMISE_REJECTED, "reason": r ]) ([ "status": PROMISE_CANCELLED,
    "reason": r ])

    A cancelled element reports PROMISE_CANCELLED and carries no value, so
    `status != PROMISE_FULFILLED` is the test for "did not deliver" —
    checking only for PROMISE_REJECTED misses it.

    "Nothing rejects" holds for a synchronous callback too. One that throws
    — which an async callback cannot do, having an implicit catch — is
    reported as that element rejecting, and the elements after it are still
    started.

    The same unbounded fan-out applies as for map_async(); batch a large
    array.

### PARAMETERS

    src    (mixed *)
           Array to fan out over.

    fun    (function)
           Function called per element, as map_async() calls it.

    extra  (mixed, optional)
           Additional arguments passed to the callback starting at $4.

### RETURN VALUES

    (mapping *) A promise for one outcome mapping per element, positionally
    matching src.

### ERRORS

    If src is not an array, or fun is not a valid function. Either rejects
    the returned promise.

### EXAMPLE

    {{di1}}foreach(mapping outcome in await settle_async(dirs, (: async_getdir($1) :)))
      if(outcome["status"] == PROMISE_FULFILLED)
        index(outcome["value"]);{{di0}}
